                        <span class="rounded-full text-primary-dark" style="background-color: #f5eefc; border-radius: 9999px; padding: 5px 10px 5px 10px; font-weight: 700; color: #7d49b1;">PLANNING YOUR MEALS</span>
                        <h3 style="font-weight: bold;">How to eat the right amount for your goals</h3>
                        <p>To track your intake and adjust your meals you can either count calories and macros or use our go-to hand portion method. (The hand portion method is simple, flexible, and has worked wonders for over 100,000 clients we've coached.)</p>

                        <div class="row">
                            <div class="card col-6">
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <div class="row">
                                        <img src="{{ asset('medicity/assets/img/cacl-hand.jpg') }}" alt="" style = "width: 150px;">
                                        <p class="mt-3 mb-0" style="font-weight: bold;">RECOMMEND $ EASY TO USE</p>
                                        <h3 style="font-weight: bold;">Hand portion-measuring system</h3>
                                        <p>Use your palm to define protein portions, a fist for vegetables, a cupped hand for carbs, and your thumb to measure fats.</p>

                                        <a href="#view_hand_method" data-bs-toggle="modal">Read more about this method</a>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="card col-6">
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <div class="row">
                                        <img src="{{ asset('medicity/assets/img/cacl-cacl.jpg') }}" alt="" style = "width: 150px;">
                                        <p class="mt-3 mb-0" style="font-weight: bold;">HARDER BUT MORE PRECISE</p>
                                        <h3 style="font-weight: bold;">Counting your calories and macros</h3>
                                        <p>Read nutrition labels and utilize tools like scales and measuring cups, or employ nutrition tracking apps, such as MyFitnessPal or Cronometer.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
